{"black_box_warning":{"current_value":"Populated FYCOMPA serious psychiatric and behavioral reactions boxed-warning text in row, with both full-warning and highlights wording concatenated.","fda_source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/202834Orig1s019lbl.pdf","https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.generic_name%3A%22perampanel%22+OR+openfda.brand_name%3A%22perampanel%22+OR+openfda.substance_name%3A%22perampanel%22&limit=10"],"proposed_value":"No boxed-warning text change required; replace the source citation with an FDA source only.","rationale":"FDA labeling supports the FYCOMPA boxed warning for serious psychiatric and behavioral reactions. The row source is not acceptable for this field because it cites DailyMed; black-box verification must cite FDA/openFDA, FDA labels, or Drugs@FDA.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified"},"blocking_questions":[],"fact_checks":[{"current_value":"perampanel","field":"generic_name","proposed_value":"perampanel","rationale":"FDA labeling identifies FYCOMPA as perampanel.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/202834Orig1s019lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"","field":"alternate_generic_names","proposed_value":"","rationale":"No separate alternate generic name was identified. E2007 is a development code and is appropriately handled as a search alias rather than an alternate generic name.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT00144690","https://www.fda.gov/files/drugs/published/202834-Perampanel-Clinical-PREA.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Fycompa","field":"trade_names","proposed_value":"Fycompa","rationale":"FDA labeling lists FYCOMPA as the brand/trade name for perampanel tablets and oral suspension.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/202834Orig1s019lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"E2007","field":"pubmed_search_aliases","proposed_value":"E2007","rationale":"E2007 is used in ClinicalTrials.gov and FDA review materials for perampanel development studies.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT00144690","https://www.fda.gov/files/drugs/published/202834-Perampanel-Clinical-PREA.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Yes","field":"available_in_us","proposed_value":"Yes","rationale":"FDA labeling and Drugs@FDA/accessdata materials support current U.S. approval/availability.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/202834Orig1s019lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"2012","field":"year_fda_cleared","proposed_value":"2012","rationale":"FDA labeling states Initial U.S. Approval: 2012, so the deterministic warning that 2012 was not concordant should not be applied.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/202834Orig1s019lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/appletter/2012/202834Orig1s000ltr.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Tablet; oral suspension","field":"formulations_available","proposed_value":"Tablet; oral suspension","rationale":"FDA label lists tablets and oral suspension.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/202834Orig1s019lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Focal; Primary generalized tonic-clonic","field":"epilepsy_type","proposed_value":"Focal; Primary generalized tonic-clonic","rationale":"FDA indications cover partial-onset/focal seizures and adjunctive therapy for primary generalized tonic-clonic seizures.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/202834Orig1s019lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"12 mg/day","field":"maximum_approved_daily_dose","proposed_value":"12 mg/day","rationale":"FDA dosing allows escalation up to 12 mg once daily when tolerated, with lower maximums in hepatic impairment.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/202834Orig1s019lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"4 mg/day for focal seizures; titrate by seizure type and response","field":"minimum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"4 mg/day for focal seizures; titrate by seizure type and response","rationale":"FDA clinical-studies section reports statistically significant seizure-rate decreases at 4-12 mg/day; label dosing otherwise starts at 2 mg and titrates by response/tolerability.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/202834Orig1s019lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Adults/adolescents: 4-12 mg once daily at bedtime","field":"typical_doses_per_day","proposed_value":"Adults/adolescents: 4-12 mg once daily at bedtime","rationale":"This is a reasonable simplified maintenance-dose range; FDA labeling gives 8-12 mg for focal maintenance with some response at 4 mg, and 8 mg for PGTC with possible increase to 12 mg.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/202834Orig1s019lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"~105 h","field":"half_life_range","proposed_value":"~105 h","rationale":"FDA pharmacokinetics section states the half-life is about 105 hours.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/202834Orig1s019lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Liver","field":"major_organ_for_metabolism","proposed_value":"Liver","rationale":"FDA labeling describes extensive metabolism via oxidation and glucuronidation, primarily mediated by CYP3A4/5, with in vitro human liver microsome data.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/202834Orig1s019lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Weak CYP3A inducer at higher doses; CYP3A substrate","field":"enzyme_inducing_or_inhibiting","proposed_value":"Weak CYP3A inducer at higher doses; CYP3A substrate","rationale":"FDA labeling supports CYP3A4/5 metabolism and weak CYP3A4/5 induction; CYP3A inducers reduce perampanel exposure.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/202834Orig1s019lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Noncompetitive antagonist of ionotropic AMPA glutamate receptors on postsynaptic neurons; precise human antiepileptic mechanism is still described as unknown in labeling.","field":"mechanism_of_action","proposed_value":"Noncompetitive antagonist of ionotropic AMPA glutamate receptors on postsynaptic neurons; precise human antiepileptic mechanism is still described as unknown in labeling.","rationale":"FDA clinical pharmacology supports both the AMPA-receptor antagonist description and that the precise human antiepileptic mechanism is unknown.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/202834Orig1s019lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"mechanism_source","proposed_value":"FDA/Drugs@FDA labeling","rationale":"The mechanism is supported by FDA labeling; DailyMed should be removed from the named source to keep sources within the trusted-source policy.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/202834Orig1s019lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"FDA label","field":"mechanism_source_tier","proposed_value":"FDA label","rationale":"The cited mechanism source tier is correct.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/202834Orig1s019lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"No clinically meaningful QT effect established","field":"qt_interval_effect","proposed_value":"No clinically meaningful QT effect established","rationale":"FDA labeling states a placebo-controlled thorough-QT study found no clinically significant QT prolongation at 6 or 12 mg, and no clinically relevant QTc prolongation at 12 mg.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/202834Orig1s019lbl.pdf","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26088895/"]},{"current_value":"CNS: dizziness 32-43%, CNS: somnolence 11-18%, constitutional: fatigue 12-15%, psychiatric: irritability 11-12%, injury: falls 7-10%, GI: nausea 7-8%","field":"adverse_symptoms_percentages","proposed_value":"CNS: dizziness 32-43%, CNS: somnolence 11-18%, constitutional: fatigue 12-15%, psychiatric: irritability 11-12%, injury: falls 7-10%, GI: nausea 7-8%","rationale":"The ranges match FDA placebo-controlled trial tables when using high-dose focal-seizure data and PGTC 8 mg data for the named adverse reactions.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/202834Orig1s019lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed SPL; status=boxed_warning_found; setid=71cf3309-e182-473c-8b0b-280cabd0e122; published=Jan 28, 2026; title=FYCOMPA (PERAMPANEL) TABLET FYCOMPA (PERAMPANEL) SUSPENSION [EISAI INC.]; url=https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=71cf3309-e182-473c-8b0b-280cabd0e122","field":"fda_black_box_warning_source","proposed_value":"FDA/Drugs@FDA label; status=boxed_warning_found; application=NDA 202834; label=2024/202834Orig1s019lbl.pdf; title=FYCOMPA (perampanel) tablets/oral suspension; url=https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/202834Orig1s019lbl.pdf","rationale":"DailyMed is not permissible for FDA boxed-warning verification under the audit policy. FDA accessdata label supports the boxed warning.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/202834Orig1s019lbl.pdf","https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.generic_name%3A%22perampanel%22+OR+openfda.brand_name%3A%22perampanel%22+OR+openfda.substance_name%3A%22perampanel%22&limit=10"]},{"current_value":"NCBI LiverTox anticonvulsants table; Epilepsy Society ASM list; Epilepsy Foundation Australia ASM list; FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"evidence_sources","proposed_value":"FDA/Drugs@FDA labeling; NCBI LiverTox; PubMed placebo-controlled RCTs; ClinicalTrials.gov trial records","rationale":"The current field includes non-trusted or non-preferred sources for this audit and does not name PubMed/ClinicalTrials sources supporting RCT and outcome cells. DailyMed should not be used for boxed-warning verification.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/202834Orig1s019lbl.pdf","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/39576191/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29250772/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27221398/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26296511/","https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT00144690"]},{"current_value":"filter fields populated for availability, enzyme effect, epilepsy type, formulation, mechanism, metabolism, QT effect, and symptom category","field":"filter_*","proposed_value":"No filter text change required after source updates.","rationale":"The filter values are concordant with the verified source facts above.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/202834Orig1s019lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Current ASM for focal-onset and primary generalized tonic-clonic seizures.","field":"status_or_notes","propose